notes.organize_table:
Four items, each counted when still (moved under 2 mm since the previous check):
- alarm clock: centre 22.5–30 cm above the drawer cabinet's base (on top of the cabinet), upright within 15°;
- figurine: centre 0.5 to 10 cm above the stand's centre point and within 2 to 4.5 cm of it seen from above (the limit depends on the figurine), upright within 15°;
- mouse: centre inside the mouse pad's footprint (above its bottom), its heading kept: right side up, its length pointing toward the robots within 45°, the same end toward the robots as at the start;
- keyboard: flat within 15°, not turned more than 45° from its start heading, its footprint covering the whole 20 cm x 6 cm rectangle centred on the frame (long side left-right).
Success (score 100%) is checked after every action, all conditions at one moment, and ends the episode: all four items; both arms home (each gripper within 15 cm of its start position on every axis and within 20° of its start orientation). No gripper condition.
Partial score (only without success), both grippers at least 80% open: 1 item 25, 2 items 50, 3 items 75, 4 items 100. Tiers latch: checked in order, at most one new tier per action, never lost; 100 is paid only with success, else 75.
Step limit: 1000 actions.
